# History files
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history

# Session Data files
.RData
.RDataTmp

# Data, figures, models directories.
#
# `/data`, not `data/*` and not bare `data`. Both parts of that matter:
#
#   data/*   ignores a directory's CONTENTS but not the path itself, so a
#            SYMLINK named `data` is an ordinary file to git and shows up as
#            untracked forever. That is the normal setup in a git worktree —
#            the cache lives in the main checkout and the worktree gets a
#            symlink so scripts resolve `data/cache/...` unchanged.
#
#   data     (bare, no slash) matches at ANY DEPTH, so it also swallows
#            `analysis/models`, and new files there become invisible to git
#            with no error — only a refusal to stage. `models/*` was safe from
#            this by accident: a pattern containing a slash is already anchored
#            to this directory.
#
#   /data    anchored to the repo root AND matches the path however it is
#            realised, directory or symlink. Both properties, no side effects.
#
# No `!data/...` negation exists here. If one is ever needed, git will not
# descend into an ignored directory, so that line must go back to `data/*`
# with the negation beneath it.
/data
/figures
/models


# User-specific files
.Ruserdata

